WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.530
This video shows where a run writes its
sediment in three places:

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:07.190
the land, the channels and the basin
outlet.

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:12.617
The run of this video is the run of Run
streamflow:

00:00:12.617 --> 00:00:18.800
the basin 02070002, 2000 to 2015, with a
warm-up of three years.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.140
The page draws no chart of sediment,

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.170
so this chapter reads the tables of the
run folder.

00:00:24.671 --> 00:00:28.661
The run of Run streamflow already wrote
the three files of this chapter.

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:30.271
No new run is needed.

00:00:30.771 --> 00:00:34.346
For the land, the row of Output tables is
Entire basin,

00:00:34.346 --> 00:00:36.231
Sediment and nutrients, Year.

00:00:36.733 --> 00:00:39.713
For the channels, it is Channels, Every
channel, Year.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.730
In Results, click Open output folder.

00:00:48.309 --> 00:00:51.709
The output folder of the run now holds
these three files.

00:00:52.209 --> 00:00:54.970
The first holds the sediment yield of the
land:

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:58.319
the sediment that leaves the land of the
basin in a year.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:02.010
The second holds the sediment budget of
every channel.

00:01:02.512 --> 00:01:04.888
The record of the basin outlet holds the

00:01:04.888 --> 00:01:07.502
sediment that passes the outlet on each
day.

00:01:08.003 --> 00:01:11.313
The chapter adds up each of the three for
every printed year.
